x}=\\frac{1}{f(x)},$ then $f(x)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the denominator using $1-{cos}^{2}⁡x={sin}^{2}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the denominator as difference of squares, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}{(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}}{\\cancel{(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-65293/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b05f4be1-95d4-5137-bbaa-71c95862bb59"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-65293"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119866/selection/1c45ea2f3a0d332cc3901ef48c5d5ba25ed2f20416671931222b3b0d2648578a" :answer/id #uuid "4ca0dd09-6e25-5bee-a23b-0c57f4f75249" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119866/selection/75e966a535fd9c2632b536ea7fb82c4c255787b492683b5f0c984313b2fc9189" :answer/id #uuid "23189c1b-74a4-50e4-9028-6d663e2f2d24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119866/selection/9a5b9390951266e2b813845cd5600199a8290221a77f4aeaff79c847a3abed64" :answer/id #uuid "694cb260-f7a1-547d-a315-72ae5e0e2759" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119866/selection/a87ad24b8b455e65e9d108aa6fbac9dfbb329fb445767b87a566d45e9db75ff8" :answer/id #uuid "a82ff050-5a53-53c0-9141-19021f3d4e04" :answer/type :answer.type/mat